{#- Heading shared by the inner pages, in the style of the home page: title,
    intro and a tilted photo. Set before including it:
    - heroText: the intro (HTML)
    - heroAlt: alt text for the page's `image`
    - heroCta / heroCtaHref: optional button under the intro
    The title shares its row with the photo, so it is sized to its column:
    the home page's text-5xl from lg, and below that 10% of the column width
    (`cqi`), capped at text-4xl. That keeps "Veranstaltungen", the longest word
    so far, on one line down to 320px wide screens; at the full-width pages'
    text-6xl it ran under the photo. Not `hyphens-auto`: it also splits words
    that would fit on the next line ("getra-gen"). `break-words` only cuts a
    word wider than the whole column, should the CMS ever get a longer one. -#}
<div class="max-w-(--breakpoint-lg) w-full mx-auto px-4 mt-10 md:mt-16 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-12 md:items-center">
  <div class="{{ 'md:w-3/5' if image else 'md:w-2/3' }} @container flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h1 class="font-bold font-hany text-[length:min(var(--text-4xl),10cqi)] lg:text-5xl leading-tight text-black break-words">
      {{ title }}
    </h1>
    <div class="text-sm md:text-base text-black space-y-3">
      {{ heroText | safe }}
    </div>
    {% if heroCtaHref %}
    <div>
      <a
        href="{{ heroCtaHref }}"
        class="inline-block border border-black rounded-xl px-3 py-1 transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-black hover:text-white"
      >{{ heroCta }}</a>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if image %}
  <div class="md:w-2/5 px-4 md:px-0">
    <div class="border-2 border-black rounded-xl overflow-hidden rotate-3">
      {% image image, heroAlt, 600, "w-full h-auto" %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
